 "result": "The session's JSON serializer wraps non-JSON types in single-key dicts, which the same serializer unwraps on load.\n\n**Wiring (`src/tessel/sessions.py`):**\n- `session_json_serializer = TypedCookieSerializer()` (L273) is the default.\n- `SignedCookieSessionInterface.serializer` (L300) points at it.\n- `make_signer` (L303) passes it to itsdangerous' `URLSafeTimedSerializer` (L313-316), which signs and encodes the cookie payload.\n\n**Tagging (`src/tessel/json/tag.py`):**\n- `TypedCookieSerializer` (L219) keeps an ordered list of tag classes.\n  - `dumps` (L321) runs `tag()` (L289), which picks the first tag whose `check()` matches and returns `{key: to_json(value)}`.\n  - `loads` (L325) runs `untag()` (L297). For a single-key dict, it looks up that key and calls the matching tag's `to_python()`.\n  - `register()` (L256) adds custom tags.\n- `TypeMarker` (L60) is the base class. Each subclass defines `key`, `check`, `to_json` and `to_python`.\n- Concrete tags:\n  - `TagTuple`: key `\" t\"`, converts to a list and back to a tuple.\n  - `TagBytes`: key `\" b\"`, base64-encodes.\n  - `TagDateTime`: key `\" d\"`, uses an HTTP date string.\n  - Others: `TagUUID` (`\" u\"`), `TagMarkup` (`\" m\"`), `TagDict` (`\" di\"`, escapes user dicts that look like tags) and `PassDict`/`PassList` (recurse into containers).",
